  "notes": [
    "Game axes: X = Blender +X, Y = Blender +Z, Z = Blender -Y; pose bones use YZX Euler = three.js XYZ.",
    "Head pivot at the skull base (back of the neck, chin height), not the head centre; neck at the collar.",
    "Lids are rigid shells about their bone world X axis (a radius per vertex): blink +1.22 closes, +0.488 is the happy squint, lidD -0.1 neutral, -0.24 happy. Their pivots sit behind the eyes (a 13 cm opening needs an 11+ cm hinge for 1.22 rad), not at the eyeball centres.",
    "The mouth parting was cut in the model (round 2); the lower copies are jaw-side, the corners shared (sealed). A closed cavity pocket on the parting, a tongue on its floor (jaw).",
    "Weights quantized to an exact 255 sum; <= 4 influences. Ears: head (root) -> ear -> earTip (the hanging lobe below the fold).",
    "The kimono skirt follows the hips with its front / side / back partly on the thighs (34 / 22 / 30% at the hem); the trouser legs follow their own thighs (the top on the hips, the hem 45% shin).",
    "The sleeves follow the upper arms (the root on the chest, the opening 40% forearm); the obi and its back knot are rigid-ish on spine / hips.",
    "The kerchief follows the chest, riding with the neck (ring top 30%, knot 35%, leaf roots 25%); the ears: head (the root rings in the skull) -> ear_ -> earTip_ over the top half.",
    "The lash rolls (Kaede_lash_L/R) are 100% lidU_*; the lids are painted per side from the skin under them.",
    "The tail: tail1 at its root under the obi (the root rings share the hips), tail2-4 along the centreline, tail4 near the cream tip."
  ]
}